Pre-existing, unrelated, low-severity — found during NEARS-3218 QA (2026-09-08, emulator-5558).
NOT caused by NEARS-3218's diff: order_tracking_screen.dart is untouched by this ticket.

Symptom: on landing on the post-place-order OrderTrackingScreen, `LocationController.getCurrentLocation`
times out fetching a live GPS fix from the emulator (despite an earlier `adb emu geo fix` call) and
falls back to a default position. This IS correctly logged via AppLogger (no silent-failure
contract violation):
  [FAIL] endpoint=null http_status=null type=GetPositionFailure msg="location: getPosition threw
  (TimeoutException) — falling back to default position"
Observed identically on both order 91213 (11:21:28) and order 91214 (11:25:25).

Likely emulator GPS-provider timing flakiness (geo fix sets a location but geolocator's
getCurrentPosition() query can still time out against it on this AVD), not a functional defect in
the ticket's scope. Logging non-blocking follow-up only.
